## 2. All FBIO ioctl Commands Defined

From `/data/vela/nuttx/include/nuttx/video/fb.h`:

| ioctl | Purpose | Argument |
|---|---|---|
| `FBIOGET_VIDEOINFO` | Get display resolution, format, plane count | `struct fb_videoinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOGET_PLANEINFO` | Get framebuffer address, stride, bpp | `struct fb_planeinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOGET_CMAP` | Get color map | `struct fb_cmap_s *` |
| `FBIOPUT_CMAP` | Set color map | `const struct fb_cmap_s *` |
| `FBIOGET_CURSOR` | Get cursor attributes | `struct fb_cursorattrib_s *` |
| `FBIOPUT_CURSOR` | Set cursor attributes | `const struct fb_setcursor_s *` |
| `FBIO_UPDATE` | Update a rectangular region | `const struct fb_area_s *` |
| `FBIO_WAITFORVSYNC` | Wait for vertical sync | `0` |
| `FBIOGET_OVERLAYINFO` | Get overlay info | `struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIO_SELECT_OVERLAY` | Select active overlay | `unsigned long` (overlay number) |
| `FBIOSET_TRANSP` | Set overlay transparency | `const struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_CHROMAKEY` | Set overlay chroma key | `const struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_COLOR` | Set overlay solid color | `const struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_BLANK` | Blank/unblank overlay | `const struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_AREA` | Set active overlay area | `const struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_DESTAREA` | Set destination area on primary FB | `const struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_BLIT` | Blit between overlays | `const struct fb_overlayblit_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_BLEND` | Blend between overlays | `const struct fb_overlayblend_s *` |
| `FBIOPAN_OVERLAY` | Pan display for overlay | `const struct fb_overlayinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOSET_POWER` | Set panel power | `int` |
| `FBIOGET_POWER` | Get panel power | `int *` |
| `FBIOSET_FRAMERATE` | Set frame rate | `int` |
| `FBIOGET_FRAMERATE` | Get frame rate | `int *` |
| `FBIOPAN_DISPLAY` | Pan display (double buffer) | `const struct fb_planeinfo_s *` |
| `FBIOPAN_CLEAR` | Clear pan buffer | `unsigned long` |
| `FBIOSET_VSYNCOFFSET` | Set VSync offset in usec | `int` |
| **`FBIOGET_VSCREENINFO`** | Linux-compat: get variable screen info | `struct fb_var_screeninfo *` |
| **`FBIOGET_FSCREENINFO`** | Linux-compat: get fixed screen info | `struct fb_fix_screeninfo *` |

