## 6. LCD Character Driver: `/data/vela/nuttx/drivers/lcd/lcd_dev.c`

For `/dev/lcd0`, the ioctl commands are different from the framebuffer ones. Key commands handled by `lcddev_ioctl`:

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `LCDDEVIO_GETRUN` | Read a row of pixels |
| `LCDDEVIO_PUTRUN` | Write a row of pixels |
| `LCDDEVIO_GETAREA` | Read a rectangular area |
| `LCDDEVIO_PUTAREA` | Write a rectangular area |
| `LCDDEVIO_GETPOWER` | Get backlight power |
| `LCDDEVIO_SETPOWER` | Set backlight power |
| `LCDDEVIO_GETCONTRAST` | Get contrast |
| `LCDDEVIO_SETCONTRAST` | Set contrast |
| `LCDDEVIO_GETPLANEINFO` | Get plane info (`struct lcd_planeinfo_s`) |
| `LCDDEVIO_GETVIDEOINFO` | Get video info (same `struct fb_videoinfo_s`) |
| `LCDDEVIO_SETPLANENO` | Select a different plane |
| `LCDDEVIO_GETFRAMERATE` | Get frame rate |
| `LCDDEVIO_SETFRAMERATE` | Set frame rate |
| `LCDDEVIO_GETAREAALIGN` | Get area alignment constraints |

The LCD dev driver does NOT support mmap -- it uses putrun/getrun transfer APIs instead.

---

## 7. Linux-Compat ioctls: `FBIOGET_VSCREENINFO` and `FBIOGET_FSCREENINFO`

Defined in `/data/vela/nuttx/include/nuttx/video/fb.h` (lines 315-320) and implemented in `/data/vela/nuttx/drivers/video/fb.c` (lines 1013-1150).

These are Linux framebuffer compatibility interfaces. The driver internally reads `fb_videoinfo_s` and `fb_planeinfo_s` and translates them:

```c
case FBIOGET_VSCREENINFO:
    // Build fb_var_screeninfo from vinfo + pinfo
    varinfo->xres           = vinfo.xres;
    varinfo->yres           = vinfo.yres;
    varinfo->xres_virtual   = pinfo.xres_virtual;
    varinfo->yres_virtual   = pinfo.yres_virtual;
    varinfo->bits_per_pixel = pinfo.bpp;
    varinfo->grayscale      = FB_ISMONO(vinfo.fmt);
    // Also fills fb_bitfield for red, green, blue, transp based on vinfo.fmt
    break;

case FBIOGET_FSCREENINFO:
    fixinfo->smem_start  = (unsigned long)pinfo.fbmem;
    fixinfo->smem_len    = pinfo.fblen;
    fixinfo->type        = FB_TYPE_PACKED_PIXELS;  // or INTERLEAVED_PLANES
    fixinfo->visual      = FB_VISUAL_TRUECOLOR;    // or MONO10
    fixinfo->line_length = pinfo.stride;
    break;
```

